- Every tool result is capped at 16 KiB (16,384 bytes). Bash output at or below 16 KiB (16,384 bytes) is returned unchanged, and an empty result stays empty. `execute_script` output above that limit is truncated on a UTF-8 character boundary; the marker reports the exact omitted bytes, so filter results in JavaScript when a returned value may be large. `execute_script` output is never spilled.
